      "question": {
        ":question/id": "4b79bc43-a386-5a26-8d0e-8a9d180ffc6c",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(3 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3 x + 3$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(3 x + 3 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{4 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{4 \\cot{\\left(3 x + 3 \\right)}}{3}+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "bc0e3fba-d493-5233-ad84-cc68f3ace337",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
