        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\cot{\\left(3 - 4 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(3 - 4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3 - 4 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\cot{\\left(3 - 4 x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(3 - 4 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{\\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\csc{\\left(3 - 4 x \\right)}}{2}+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
