        ":question/id": "a9bd005b-6418-57af-a882-7141e88f9979",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cot{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cot{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)} \\csc{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cot{\\left(u \\right)} \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\csc{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\csc{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=1,\\quad \\csc{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}=2$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\frac{\\csc{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}=\\left(1\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "d084e1ed-d542-54ac-8e98-d5a3a1b53581",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "cef0d8a8-fe8f-5015-b7e2-cc307e60aa68",
