      "question": {
        ":question/id": "faef1f10-e898-55db-9c5f-90f5c88abaa0",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\\\x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe new bounds decrease. Keep this order when evaluating the antiderivative.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} 4 \\csc^{2}{\\left(- 2 x + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-2\\left(\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nEndpoint values: $\\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\right)}=0,\\quad \\cot{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}=1$.\n\nIntegrate and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\left[2 \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\left(2\\right)-\\left(0\\right).\n$$\n\nThe answer is\n\n$$\n2.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "81c4cf15-4b50-5284-8986-63a961b5ceda",
