      "question": {
        ":question/id": "c06358ca-e05b-557c-8e09-11accb28a69a",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(2 - 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2 - 2 x$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-2.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\csc^{2}{\\left(2 - 2 x \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the integration rule:\n\n$$\n\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=- \\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-\\left(\\int \\csc^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\cot{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\cot{\\left(2 - 2 x \\right)}+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "555a06df-3e05-59c9-98a2-f1c42bd7e052",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
